## Context

The doc has matured from intellectual scaffolding into a thesis: the
four limits split 2/2 between data and answer; method quality is a
perpendicular axis; the regimes-scatter ladder visits each limit;
deep research saturates data and answer quality. This is no longer
a "framework" — it's an argument the paper makes.

Rename to reflect the upgrade. Done after 0145 confirms the
argument is coherent with the project's quality-grounding doc, so
we don't commit to an "argument" label on a doc that turns out to
have a load-bearing inconsistency.

## Actions

1. `git mv docs/measurement-framework.md docs/argument.md`.
2. Update doc title: "The argument: axes, lenses, three qualities"
   or similar. Update the working-note disclaimer at the top.
3. Update internal cross-references (slides, other docs, ticket
   bodies referencing the old path, `capability-timeline.md`
   backlink).
4. `grep -rn 'measurement-framework' .` → 0 hits after the pass.
5. Update `STATE.md` if it mentions the framework.

## Exit criteria

- File renamed; git history preserved (`git log --follow
  docs/argument.md` still works).
- All cross-references updated.
- Title and intro paragraph reflect "argument" framing.
- No build breakage from broken references.
